# Variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ are baked directly into the JS bundle at
# build time. Never put a secret here - see docs/developer-guide.md.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_RELAY_URL=wss://relay.example.com

# Crash reporting (Sentry). Unset in a source build, which is the point:
# without it src/observability/crashReporting.ts never calls Sentry.init(),
# so a build made from this repo collects and sends nothing. CI injects it
# from the GitHub repository VARIABLE `SENTRY_DSN` (deliberately a variable
# and not a secret, so it can be read back to confirm which project a build
# reports to) for official builds only. A DSN is a write-only ingest key
# rather than a secret, but it is still not committed, because a fork's
# crashes would otherwise land in (and exhaust) Kangentic's free-tier Sentry
# quota. Set it locally only to test the reporting path itself; note that
# without SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN below, that local build uploads no source map,
# so the frames of any test crash arrive unsymbolicated.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplekey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0

# Uploads source maps and debug symbols at build time, and is what makes
# app.config.ts include the Sentry config plugin at all. A real secret:
# never commit it. Only needed when producing a release build you want
# symbolicated.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Reveals a "Crash reporting test" section in Settings (a JS-throw row and a
# native-crash row) and turns on Sentry's `debug: true` native logging. Set
# only when deliberately verifying what a crash report contains; never in a
# store build. build-android.yml's crash_test dispatch input is the normal
# way to set it - never in eas.json. That workflow refuses a run that also
# names a submit_track, so a crash-test build cannot reach a Play track.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_KANGENTIC_CRASHTEST=1
